  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">White Emergency flood response - CRS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to provide emergency assistance for the flood affected victims in White Nile State. The emergency is beyond the responding capacity of the government in White Nile state, and thus complementary assistance by organisations operating in the area was requested by state. CAFOD intervention will be providing Non Food Items (NFIs) with the aim of restoring social life of the affected population. This response will  benefit 779 families (4,674 people) with culturally appropriate lifesaving  NFIs in White Nile state. The specific needs of women and children will be considered while deciding which NFIs to purchase and distribute to the community. The financial support is from Catholic Relief Services (CRS) Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
